content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22871, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is 7.6 mm/s at the drive-end bearing housing. Figure 3 is the applicable HF-300 criterion for vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings: 7.6 exceeds the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary and falls within Zone D (7.1–11.0 mm/s), the highest severity zone, labelled 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. SSP-07 therefore requires immediate shutdown and notification of the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 84 C. The HF-300 housing-surface temperature limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. Thus 84 C is 14 C above normal, 4 C above the alarm limit and 6 C below the trip limit. Because the manufacturer's alarm limit is exceeded, SSP-07 requires a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Water leakage from the shaft area at approximately one drop per second matches the manual's 'leakage at shaft seal' symptom, for which it directs mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check. The evidence supplies no numerical allowable leakage-rate limit against which to assess the one-drop-per-second reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The approximately 10-minute dry run was not permissible: the HF-300 has Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and the manual states 'never run dry'. No nonzero allowable dry-running duration is documented.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal face damage from dry running is the leading suspected cause of the shaft-area leakage. The troubleshooting table lists worn or cracked seal faces and a seal run dry as probable causes; the recent 10-minute dry run also violated the explicit never-run-dry requirement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear and/or shaft misalignment could explain the high vibration and high bearing temperature. Both are listed causes of those two symptoms, and misalignment is also a listed cause of shaft-seal leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the original HF3-450 component seal is still fitted, its bulletin-identified early failure associated with the revised sleeve tolerance is another possible cause. SB-2026-014 covers serial HF3-22000 and above, and HF3-22871 is within that range.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Other documented possibilities requiring inspection are impeller imbalance or damage and cavitation for the high vibration, and over-greasing for the high bearing temperature. The troubleshooting table accordingly calls for bearing and impeller inspection, an NPSH check, a grease-quantity check and alignment checks.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-104 immediately and keep it stopped because the reported vibration is in manufacturer severity Zone D. Notify the reliability engineer before any restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before internal pump, seal or bearing work, electrically isolate and apply LOTO at the MCC; mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves; drain and vent the pump and then obtain the required line-break permit. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because P-104 is within the chemically dosed P-101 to P-106 filtered-water pump group using sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Prepare the back pull-out removal as a 68 kg lift: obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment. After isolation and draining, remove the back pull-out assembly; its design permits removal without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, withdraw the mechanical seal and shaft sleeve, and inspect the sleeve for scoring.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate the vibration and temperature before reassembly: check grease quantity, inspect both bearings and the impeller, and check NPSH. Use the findings to distinguish bearing wear, over-greasing, impeller imbalance or damage, and cavitation; alignment is checked later in this sequence.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Measure the sleeve scoring depth and replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Fit one new HF3-450B cartridge seal and a new HF3-120 casing gasket; do not fit HF3-450. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed to set the seal, but the scoring inspection and 0.1 mm replacement criterion still apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace drive-end bearing HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive-end bearing HF3-510 (6310-C3) as a pair, one of each. Procedure 5.3 requires pair replacement when either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature; this pump has a reported high drive-end bearing-housing temperature of 84 C. Retain the grease-quantity, wear and misalignment checks to address the underlying cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble using the applicable torques. For Table 5 fasteners with lightly oiled threads, tighten disturbed M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, the M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm and disturbed M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm. Tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm under SB-2026-014; do not use the superseded 25 Nm value.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Perform laser shaft alignment after the bearing-housing work and after any movement of the motor or bearing housing. The applicable tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, confirm that the reliability engineer has been notified. On restart, inspect and record shaft-seal leakage, bearing-housing vibration and bearing-housing temperature, and compare them again with Figure 3 and the 70/80/90 C normal/alarm/trip limits. Stop the pump immediately if vibration is again in Zone D; no numerical post-repair leakage acceptance limit is supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; use instead of HF3-450 on this serial-range pump. One seal is required, and its gland-nut torque is 30 Nm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit a new gasket during mechanical-seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; replace together with HF3-510 as a bearing pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace together with HF3-512 as a bearing pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, conditional part: install one replacement only if inspection finds scoring deeper than 0.1 mm; otherwise retain the serviceable sleeve.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Immediate machine stop is mandatory because 7.6 mm/s is in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D. Notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves: P-104 is one of the P-101 to P-106 filtered-water pumps identified as chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds the 25 kg lifting threshold. Use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Raise the priority-1 work order within the shift because the 84 C bearing-housing temperature exceeds the manufacturer's 80 C alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: standard time 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair: standard time 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard time 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal-part conflict: the manual parts list identifies HF3-450, but SB-2026-014 says not to fit HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward and specifies HF3-450B instead. P-104 is serial HF3-22871, so the bulletin applies and HF3-450B is selected. The bulletin's provision for pumps below HF3-22000 to continue using HF3-450 does not apply to this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque conflict: manual procedure 5.2 points to Table 5, whose M10 seal-gland-nut torque is 25 Nm, while SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B and identifies 25 Nm as the former value. Because HF3-22871 is within the bulletin's serial range and will receive HF3-450B, use 30 Nm. Table 5 remains applicable to the other listed fasteners.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the reported 7.6 mm/s vibration measurement recorded as RMS, as specified for Figure 3? The fault report gives mm/s and the bearing-housing location but does not explicitly state RMS.",
    "Which seal is currently installed, HF3-450 or HF3-450B, and has SB-2026-014 previously been incorporated? This affects assessment of the bulletin-related failure mechanism but not the specified replacement part.",
    "Does shaft-sleeve scoring exceed 0.1 mm, and do the bearing, impeller, grease and NPSH inspections reveal additional damage or require further parts? These findings are unavailable until strip-down and inspection.",
    "What numerical shaft-seal leakage rate is acceptable after repair? The evidence identifies the leakage symptom and corrective action but provides no leakage-rate limit.",
    "What acceptance value or site criterion should be used for the manual's NPSH check? No NPSH limit is included in the evidence."
  ]
}
